        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Madagascar</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">5 May to 6 November 1942: Operation <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ironclad">Ironclad</a> at Diego-Suarez from 5 to 7 May, then Operations Stream, Line and Jane from 10 September, and an armistice on 6 November</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>, from Diego-Suarez (now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antsiranana">Antsiranana</a>) at the northern tip, in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>, to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahajanga">Majunga</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toamasina">Tamatave</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antananarivo">Tananarive</a>, Tulear and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fianarantsoa">Fianarantsoa</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a>, with the landing force of Force 121 under Major-General Robert Sturges and the naval force under Rear-Admiral Edward Syfret; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vichy">Vichy</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> under Governor General Armand Léon Annet, with about 8,000 troops, about 6,000 of them Malagasy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tirailleurs">tirailleurs</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> took Diego-Suarez in three days and the rest of the island by the end of October. Fighting ceased and an armistice was granted on 6 November, and the island was placed under Free French control.</span></div>
        </div>
