    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The campaign was launched to deny <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>'s ports to the Imperial Japanese Navy and to protect Allied shipping routes to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southeast-asia">Southeast Asia</a>.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vichy">Vichy</a> garrison of about 8,000 was made up mostly of Malagasy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tirailleurs">tirailleurs</a>, and its Joffre line at Antisarane held the first assault until a destroyer landed marines in the town.</li><li>It was the first large-scale operation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> combining sea, land and air forces; Julian Jackson observed that the French held out longer in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a> in 1942 than against the Germans in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1940.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a> destroyer, HMS Anthony, dashed past the harbour defences of Antisarane and put fifty <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-marines">Royal Marines</a> ashore in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vichy">Vichy</a> rear, and the town surrendered that evening.</p></aside>
    </section>

